 and false otherwise."},"processAuctionFeeTransfer(uint256)":{"details":"Called by registerValidator() in StakingManager.sol","params":{"_bidId":"the ID of the validator"}},"proxiableUUID()":{"details":"Implementation of the ERC1822 {proxiableUUID} function. This returns the storage slot used by the implementation. It is used to validate the implementation's compatibility when performing an upgrade. IMPORTANT: A proxy pointing at a proxiable contract should not be considered proxiable itself, because this risks bricking a proxy that upgrades to it, by delegating to itself until out of gas. Thus it is critical that this function revert if invoked through a proxy. This is guaranteed by the `notDelegated` modifier."},"reEnterAuction(uint256)":{"params":{"_bidId":"the ID of the bid which was matched to the cancelled stake."}},"renounceOwnership()":{"details":"Leaves the contract without owner. It will not be possible to call `onlyOwner` functions anymore. Can only be called by the current owner. NOTE: Renouncing ownership will leave the contract without an owner, thereby removing any functionality that is only available to the owner."},"setMaxBidPrice(uint64)":{"params":{"_newMaxBidAmount":"the new amount to set the maximum bid price as"}},"setMinBidPrice(uint64)":{"params":{"_newMinBidAmount":"the new amount to set the minimum bid price as"}},"setProtocolRevenueManager(address)":{"details":"Needed to process an auction fee","params":{"_protocolRevenueManager":"the address of the protocol manager"}},"setStakingManagerContractAddress(address)":{"params":{"_stakingManagerContractAddress":"new stakingManagerContract address"}},"transferOwnership(address)":{"details":"Transfers ownership of the contract to a new account (`newOwner`). Can only be called by the current owner."},"updateAdmin(address)":{"params":{"_newAdmin":"the new address to set as admin"}},"updateSelectedBidInformation(uint256)":{"details":"Called by batchDepositWithBidIds() in StakingManager.sol","params":